      "attributes": {
        "id": 1208,
        "relationship_type": "related",
        "body": "Both use ほか (他, other) to express contrast or exclusivity. ほかに(も) and ほか(に)は mean 'other than' and are used to compare or list alternatives. をおいてほかに〜ない is a stronger expression meaning 'no one/nothing else but', as in 彼をおいてほかに適任者はいない ('There's no one more suitable than him.').",
